// Core explicit early-disposal surface.
//
// `drop<T>` consumes a whole value to end its lifetime early. Its return edge
// uses the same checked plan as scope exit: it transfers the value to the
// machine selected by `dropped by`, or disposes ordinary structural components.
// A selected machine is an ordinary by-value call target. Its complete
// consuming pattern ends the wrapper, leaving its components and their
// obligations with the consumer. Erased fields remain semantically present
// but carry no runtime representation or runtime cleanup actions.
//
// The body is empty because `value` reaches its checked cleanup edge here.
// The edge performs disposal; no authored statement calls the selected machine.

public machine drop<T>(value: T) {
}
